Fri Oct 30 10:32:14 UTC 2026 - Marcus Rueckert <mrueckert@suse.de>

- Update to version 0.29.7:
  This is a security release. It fixes findings from Anthropic's
  oss-scanner project and the Tailworm report. None are critical,
  but some can cause denial of service in Headscale. We recommend
  that all users upgrade to Headscale 0.29.7 and Tailscale v1.104.4
  or newer as soon as possible, especially those using Tailscale
  SSH.

  Tailscale v1.104.4 fixes vulnerabilities in SSH forwarding, SSH
  session handling and Serve. These fixes run in tailscaled on your
  nodes; upgrading Headscale alone does not apply them.

  See Tailscale's security bulletins and Tailscale SSH: Findings
  and fixes.

  To disable SSH agent and port forwarding on a node, set
  TS_SSH_DISABLE_FORWARDING=1 in the tailscaled service environment
  and restart the service. This setting applies to all Tailscale
  SSH sessions on that node and is also available in older clients.
  #3624

  This release also fixes the issues that oss-scanner reported in
  Headscale: ANT-2026-MLP8ZR5T, ANT-2026-LYVGXVSW,
  ANT-2026-AWGRB7O1, ANT-2026-QMCAFJ1Q, ANT-2026-RQS7JAPP,
  ANT-2026-5B6KE87K, ANT-2026-KFCFFM34, ANT-2026-K903ZEUA,
  ANT-2026-NM50ZP4N, ANT-2026-ZC18AF82, ANT-2026-NWTIBB02,
  ANT-2026-MX8FKG4K. #3603


  - Metrics are no longer exposed to unregistered clients through
    the Noise protocol. They remain available only on the
    configured metrics listener; an empty metrics_listen_addr
    disables that listener #3623
  - Update the Tailscale dependency to v1.104.4, which bounds how
    much of an unexpected DERP HTTP response is read #3577
  - Keep pending registrations and OIDC logins at capacity instead
    of evicting ones awaiting approval; new requests get a retry
    response, and registered nodes keep capacity for SSH checks
    #3586
  - Cap stored pending registration data at 64 KiB, keeping tags
    and expiry; oversized interactive registrations are rejected
    #3586
  - Check the OIDC login type before storing anything, accept each
    OIDC callback only once, and free an SSH check's slot once the
    client has read its result #3586
  - Stop serving a route that is a single address inside the node
    IP ranges, such as 100.64.0.11/32 or ::ffff:100.64.0.11/128,
    because it names a node, not a subnet; the route stays approved
    and listed, and wider routes are still served #3603
  - Require a valid pre-auth key to re-register an expired tagged
    node #3603
  - Another user's key or login on a tagged machine now creates a
    new device for that user instead of re-authenticating the
    tagged node #3603
  - Fix one node with a stored key expiry outside the years 0 to
    9999 in UTC failing the map of every node that can see it; it
    is now left out of its peers' maps and the startup check names
    it with the fix command #3603
  - Refuse a key expiry outside the years 0 to 9999 in UTC on
    registration, on the OIDC token-expiry path and in headscale
    nodes expire / POST /api/v1/node/{node_id}/expire (HTTP 400);
    the latest accepted expiry no longer fails node listings on
    PostgreSQL in a zone east of UTC #3603
  - Keep the first 256 endpoints and 4096 announced routes from
    client reports; oversized hostnames, requested tags or other
    metadata return a registration error or HTTP 413 on map
    updates. Zoned IPv6 endpoints are refused #3603
  - At startup, trim stored hostnames, endpoints and routes to the
    client-report limits and remove zoned endpoints. Hostinfo
    exceeding its size or tag limit is dropped until the next valid
    report #3603
  - Pending interactive registrations and follow-up waits keep only
    the hostname, OS and requested tags; other device details
    arrive with the first map request. Reauthentication preserves
    routes, services and endpoints #3603
  - Fix web reauthentication dropping the discovery key, so peers
    could not reach the device #3603
  - A stalled request body, or a Noise tunnel with no open request,
    is closed after 30 seconds #3603
  - A registration follow-up from a machine other than the one that
    started the registration is refused before it waits #3603
  - Only the newest follow-up waits on a pending registration or
    SSH check; older ones are answered at once #3603
  - Fix registration locks staying in memory after the registration
    ends #3603
  - Fix concurrent deletes of one node freeing its addresses and
    announcing its removal more than once #3603
  - OIDC verifies an email against the document supplying it; an
    email_verified flag without an address no longer verifies
    another document's email #3603
  - Fix release builds reporting their version with a +dirty suffix
    #3584
  - Fix SSH policy acceptEnv having no effect, so allowed
    environment variables reach SSH sessions. Upgrade SSH
    destination nodes to Tailscale v1.104.4 or newer before using
    acceptEnv, because older clients can disclose forwarded values
    #3569

