Sat Oct 24 14:04:42 UTC 2026 - Marcus Rueckert <mrueckert@suse.de>

- Update to version 0.29.6:
  Minimum supported Tailscale client version: v1.80.0

  - Security
    - Build with Go 1.27.3 to reject certificate chains containing
      the compromised eMudhra intermediate keys (CVE-2026-111943)
      Go #82345
    - Update and pin the normal and debug container bases to images
      whose CA bundles no longer include emSign ECC Root CA - G3
      #3579
    - Update golang.org/x/net to v0.60.0, golang.org/x/text to
      v0.42.0 and gRPC to v1.83.2 to address HTTP/2
      denial-of-service and text-processing vulnerabilities (x/net,
      x/text, gRPC)
    - Custom builds must be rebuilt with Go 1.27.3 or newer to
      receive the certificate-chain protection.
  - Changes
    - Speed up peer-map construction on large tailnets by finding
      each node's matching rules once, instead of checking every
      pair of nodes against every rule #3556
    - Build the peer map once per policy write instead of twice,
      and skip the rebuild when reloading an unchanged policy #3557
    - Reduce work when broadcasting map updates by avoiding
      repeated recipient filtering #3568
    - Avoid INTERNAL_ERROR stream errors when a node logs out or is
      deleted, or when Headscale shuts down; writes already in
      progress have a short grace period to finish, while clients
      that stop reading are still disconnected #3575
    - Return database-open errors instead of risking a panic or
      returning a partially initialized database handle #3496
    - Update the Tailscale dependency to v1.102.0 for Go 1.27 JSON
      compatibility in SSH check responses

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 13 15:00:27 UTC 2026 - Marcus Rueckert <mrueckert@suse.de>

- Update to version 0.29.5:
  - Fix via exit-node steering being undone by an unrelated ACL or
    grant rule that matches the viewer #3495
  - Fix via grants not offering exit nodes and subnet routes to a
    group that names an unknown user #3516
  - Fix SSH check periods and app grants dropping a group that
    names an unknown user #3516
  - Fix policy tests and sshTests failing for a group that names an
    unknown user #3516
  - Fix an unknown user in nodeAttrs rejecting the policy #3516
  - Fix every grant being fully resolved as if it had via when the
    policy has no via grants, slowing map generation on large
    tailnets #3538
  - Fix a data race in via route resolution when the policy has
    both via grants and ACLs #3515
  - Fix packet filters under autogroup:self not updating after a
    user is added or renamed #3501
  - Fix a rejected policy leaving its packet filter active #3501
  - Fix an exit node or subnet router not seeing its own approved
    routes until it reconnected, so tailscale status did not show
    it offering an exit node #3518
  - Fix deleted nodes, and peers hidden by a policy change, staying
    listed in the Tailscale Android app; removed peers are now sent
    as their own incremental map update #3492 #3527
  - Policy changes no longer resend DNS configuration to every
    node, sparing clients a full netmap rebuild; a node gets its
    DNS configuration when its own NextDNS nodeAttrs, tags or
    hostname change, which also fixes NextDNS device metadata going
    stale after a hostname change #3492
  - Fix SSH access surviving the removal of its policy rules;
    clients kept their last SSH rules, and a pending SSH check
    could still be approved #3517
  - Fix SSH check periods coming from the first check rule for a
    node pair instead of the rule for the login user #3517
  - Policy changes resend a node's SSH policy only when it changed,
    sparing clients a full netmap rebuild #3517
  - Fix SSH check accepting a repeated follow-up for an
    already-decided session, even after a rejection #3526
  - Fix an ephemeral node being deleted while online, when it
    reconnected while its previous session was being marked offline
    #3539
  - Fix peers dropping traffic from a node that re-authenticates
    after its key expired #3541
  - Fix clients uploading logs to Tailscale Inc. while
    logtail.enabled is false; clients also granted the
    data-plane-audit-logs node attribute now go down until
    tailscale up #3522
  - Fix a node ping being lost when a full map update is queued at
    the same time #3523

